      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>*ARRIN GTON BLUE COAT CHARITY SCHOOL NOTICE IS HEREBY Given, that the TRUSTEES of the above SCHOOL will, at their next „quarterly Meeting on the 18th day of October next, *Zeeed to elect One Child (1 Boy) to the Vacancy 7.1? existing in the Institution. No Candidate will be (lf!lgible unless an application on his behalf (arms of which may be obtained from the Clerk, at his rntuae, 3, Winwick Street), shall have been made to the ;:ierk to the Trustees, at least fourteen days previous 44 the day 0 fl Meetiug. mn i electing Children, the Trustees make OrPhans eir flrat choice. Those deprived of one parent come „next in consideration, and after them the children of Vreats who have the greatest number and the enderest means. Dated this 17th day of September 1909. HENRY GREENALL, Clerk tothe Trustees.</p>
        <p>RFORD BARRACKS BOXING CLUB FIRST MEETING, 1909-1910. AT GYMNASIUM, ORFORD BARRACKS,</p>
        <p>AT 7 P.M., THURSDAY, SEPTEMBER 30tb, 1909.</p>
        <p>10 Stone and under Novices' Competition, open to ;ILR civilians in Warrington and a radius of 10 miles. Antries must reach CAPTAIN MORGAN not later than BePtember 27th, at Orford Barracks, Warrington. .-.TWO COMPETITIONS open to the Club and a Ilt.rand SIX-ROUND CONTEST will also take place. 4' 411 details will be advertised later. ul?,,urther information can be bad from CAPTAIN v It, GAN, Hon. Sec., ORFORD BARRACKS, "ARRINGTON. • „Reserved Seats, 2s. Gd.; First Seats, is. Gd.; Second is.; Back Seats and standing room, Gd. ROYAL COURT THEATRE, WARRIN rEIS3-S. PROPRIETOR: MR. JOSEPH BEECHAM.</p>
        <p>GENERAL MANAGER : MR. A. M. LOADER. ACTING MANAGER: MR. NORMAN LATHAM. MONDAY NEXT, SEPTEMBER 20TH, FOR SDI NIGHTS. MATINEE, THURSDAY, AT 2.30. FIRST PRODUCTION ON ANY STAGE BY THE NATIONAL DEFENCE CO. OF THE NEW MILITARY PLAY- "A NATION IN ARMS." BY B. S. TOWNROE, POWERFUL WEST END COMPANY. MAGNIFICENT SCENERY AND EFFECTS.</p>
        <p>_ N.B.—On Monday night, to commemorate the first P.Loduction of "A Nation in Arms," a special illustrated I.I3OIIVENIR, containing an introduction by Field- -marshal Roberts, V.C., K.G., will be given away to all *lirly door patrons. All Territorials in uniform will be admitted at half- on "Territorial Night," Monday, September 20th 41 all parts. boors open at 6.45. Commence 7.30. ...Seats may be booked at the Theatre between 10 a.m. ""41 3 p.m. and 7.30 and 9.30. p.m.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <p>AATARRINGTON UNION. APPLICATIONS are invited from single women or widows, between the ages of 21 and 30 years, for the appoint- bleat of Probationer Nurse at the Union Infirmary. t Salary Ist year £9, 2nd year, £l2, 3rd year £l5, :f3gether with apartments, rations, washing, indoor 4,411f0rm and medical attendance in sickness whilst in the laospitai. ..Porms of application can be obtained from the under- Il_gned, and the application forms must be filled up in Vie candidates own writing and returned to me not 4ftter than 10 a.m. on Friday, the 24th instant. , By order,</p>
        <p>ARTHUR IiOTTOIqLEY, Union Clerk. 13esysey Chambers, Warrington: 17th,September, 1909.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <p>WARRINGTON GARDEN SUBURBS, LIMITED. SPLENDID BUILDING SITES at GRAPPENHALL and GREAT SANKEY. Special advantages; moderate ground rents.—Apply to the Secretary, ARTHUR BENNETT, Chartered Accountant, Market Gate Chambers, Warrington.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0006" n="art0006">
        <head>COUNTY OF` CHESTER.</head>
        <p>COUNTY OF` CHESTER.</p>
        <p>NORTHWICH PARLIAMENTARY DIVISION. REGISTRATION OF PARLIAMENTARY ELECTORS, COUNTY ELECTORS, AND PAROCHIAL ELECTORS. 1909.</p>
        <p>NoTict-i-S HEREBY GIVEN, that DAVID ARCHER VAUGHAN COLT WILLIAMS, ESQUIRE, having been appointed one of the Barristers to REVISE THE LISTS OF ELECTORS in Parlia- mentary Elections within the North Wales Circuit, will make a Circuit and hold Courts for Revising the Lists of Parliamentary Electors, County Electors, and Parochial Electors, and also of the Separate List of Persons entitled to be elected Members of the County Council of the County of Chester, though not entitled to be on the County Electors Roll of the said County, for the NORTHWICEI DIVISION of the COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places follow- ing that is to say:— For the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling District, viz.: MIDDLEWICH POLLING DISTRICT—Bostock, Byley ; that part formerly known as Croston and Ravenscroft ; Clive, Kinderton ; that part formerly known as Kinderton-cum-Hulme ; Middlewich and</p>
        <p>Stanthorne. ON MONDAY, the 27th day of September next, at 10 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Town Hall,</p>
        <p>Aiiddlewich. For the _several Parishes. in the following Polling</p>
        <p>_ Districts, WINSFORD (OVER) POLLING DISTRICT—Over. WINSFORD (WHARTON) POLLING DISTRICT—</p>
        <p>Wharton ON TUESDAY, the 28th day of September next, at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day. At the Magistr ates</p>
        <p>Court Houi-e, Over. For the several Parishes and parts of a Parish in the following Polling Districts, viz. : ASTON-BY-SIIT lON POLLING DISTRICr—Aston Grange, Aston-by-Sutton with Middleton Grange, Dutton and Sutton. HALTON POLLING DISTRICT—HaIton, Norton</p>
        <p>and Stockharn. RUNCORN NORTH POLLING DISTRICT—That part of Runcorn called Runcorn North. RUNCORN SOUTH POLLING DISTRICT—That part of RIMCOM called Runcorn South. WESTON POLLING DISTRICT—CIifton and</p>
        <p>Weston. ON WEDNESDAY, the 29th day of September next, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day. At the Magistrates' , Court House, Runcorn. For the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz. : BARNTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Anderton, Barn- ton, Bartington, Cogshall, Comberbach, Little Leigh</p>
        <p>and rbur-y. DAVENH AM POLLING DIST RlCT—Davenham _ . . .</p>
        <p>Eaton, Leftwich, Moulton, Whatcroft ; that part formerly known as the Parish of Whatoroft. MARSTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Budvrorth Great, Marston and Wincham. NORTHWICH (CASTLE) POLLING DISTRICT— Hartford, Northwich ; that put formerly the Urban part of Hartford and Parish of Castle Nortbwicb. NORTHWICEI(LEFTWICH)POLLING DISTRICT— Northwich that part formly the Urban part of Leftwich and Parish of Northwicb. NORTHWICH (WITTON) POLLING DISTRICT— Northwich ; that part formerly the Parish of Witton-cum-Twambrooks. WEAVERHAM POLLING DISTRICT—Acton and Weaverham-cum-Milton WINNINGTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Northwich ; that part formerly the Urban part of Winnington ; Wilmington: that part formerly the Rural part of Winnington ; Wintungton : that part formerly known as Wallerscote. And for all and every the Parishes, Townships and Places (if any) within the said Notthwich Division of the County ,of Chester, for which Courts to Revise the Parliamentary Electors' Lists, County Electors' List and Parochial Electors' Lists therein, have not herein before been appointed.</p>
        <p>On THURSDAY, the 39th day of September next, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon; and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day ; on Friday, the Ist day of October next, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon ; and on Saturday, the 2nd day of October next, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Magistrates' Court House, Northwich. N.B.—All the Lists for the Rural Parishes will be revised on Thursday, the 30th day of September, and all Overseers must attend at the morning sitting on that day. All Overseers and other persons whose attendance may be necessary, are hereby required to attend the said Courts at the several times and places aforesaid, at which the Lists of their respective Parishes are hereby appointed to be revised, and all Overseers are required to produce in Court the Rate Books of their respective Parishes' containibg the Poor Rates made and allowed during the period betwien the sth day of January, 1908, and the 15th day of July, 1909, and to bring with them copies of their Lists, and all Notices of Claims and Objections. and other papers they have received, concerning the Registration of Parliamentary Electors for the Northwich Division, and County and Parochial Electors for the said County of Chester. REGINALD POTTS, • Clerk of the Cheshire County Council. Chester, 3rd August, 1903.</p>
        <p>LANGLANDS' SAILINGS TO GREENOCK AND GLASGOW. "PRINCESS LOUISE" OR OTHER STEAMER. From LIVERPOOL From GLASGOW (Clarence dock). (Berths N 0.22-28, north side) Sat. Sept. 18th 11 p.m. Tues. Sep. 21st 2 p.m. *6.30 p.m. Thurs. Sep. 23rd 4 p.m. Sat. Sep. 25th 2 p.m. *8.30 p.m. Tues. Sep. 28th 9 p.m. Thnrs.Sep.3oth 2 p.m.*5.25 p.m. *Train from Glasgow (Central) to Greenock (Central). SPECIAL REDUCED THROUGH TICKETS from Warrington, Widnes &amp;c. Single, cabin us. 6d., Return (valid for two months) 175., Steerage, single, Os. Special 14 days Excursion Tickets: Cabin 155., Steerage Bs. 6d., including railway fare Greenock to Glasgow, or rice versa, Single Ist class and cabin ]3s., 3rd class and steerage Os. 9d. ; Return (valid for two months) Ist class and cabin 19s. 6d., Brd class and cabin 18s. 6d. M. LANGLANDS AND SONS, 14, CROSS STREET, MANCHESTER, BROWN'S BUILDINGS, EXCHANGE, LIVERPOOL</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0007" n="art0007">
        <head>THIS MAGNIFICENT NEW BUILDING</head>
        <p>THIS MAGNIFICENT NEW BUILDING</p>
        <p>WILL BE OPENED SHORTLY as a high class rink with all up-to-date requirements. The finest, best equipped rink out of London. The Empire Rink has an ideal floor, high class and well furnishei lounge, well lighted, heated and ventilated. Contracts will be very cheap.</p>
        <p>PRIVATE LESSONS by Experts at moderate charge 3. CARNIVALS, GYMKHANAS, HOCKEY MATCHES, Scc. Warrington's new public resort for old and young, well conducted on up-to-date lines. Capital accommodation for non-skaters. Splendid Promenade round the Rink. High Class Refreshments at moderate charges.</p>
        <p>SESSIONS: Morning Free, Skates 6d. Afternoon 2 to 5, entrance 6d., skates 6d. Evening 7to 10, entrance 6d., skates 6d. Persons using their own skates, entrance 6d., use of floor 6d. Special evenings each week. Further particulars as to opening Sze., in next weeks papers.</p>
      </div>
