        <head>READING.</head>
        <p>READING.</p>
        <p>Often proves to you the impe, •ctions of your sight. When it bacoms necessary to hold the book nearer to or further away from the eyes—depead up)n it something is wrong. When letters" run into one another" or the eyes ache, when fatigue follows reading, the conditions of the eyes shiuld be investigated. This is advisable, not only that your capability for rending (or sewing) may remain coo.l bat also becluse straining eyes area direct tax upon the health. We have an equipment whizh together NiLti our experience _enables as to determine exactly the state and needs of your eyes. Our charges are low.</p>
