        <p>[Cricket Notes.</p>
        <p>Warrington brought their season to a close on SAtUr- day when they entertained Sale on the Arpley enclosure. The visitors brought a strong side, but Warrington lacked the services of several of their prominent players. The encounter resulted in a draw, Sale having declared alter making 103 for 7 wickets, while Warrington had responded with 50 for 5 uickets. The feature of the match was F. C. ‘Vilde's flue display ' for Sale, his 44 being made in faultless style and inclue:ng sevtn 4's.</p>
        <p>Warrington 2nd made a poor show against Sale 2nd and had to admit defeat to the extent of 50 runs.</p>
        <p>Warrington Municipal Officers' G uild secured a victory at the expen W se of hmick Asylum Green, taPng nine wickets for 25 rir</p>
