      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0076" n="art0076">
        <head>ODDFELLOWS' BOWLING MAIN.</head>
        <p>ODDFELLOWS' BOWLING MAIN.</p>
        <p>The ac L'ond annual bowling main in connection with tbe "Haven of Rest " Lodge, 1.0.0. F., M.U.F.S., took place at Ye Old Hammers and Pincers" Hotel, Hough Green, on Saturday last when the P.G.M. of the District (Bro. G. F. Freeman) the P.C.S. (Bro. F. Webster) and several of the Oddfellows' friends were present. There were 22 entries and sore very fine games were played. P.G. John Boleswerth and P.O. James A. NVondhead met in the final and their game was watched with very great interest, Bro. Wood- hcad running out the winner by 15-14. A the main a substantial tea was partaken of in the , every praise is due to the proprietor M. for the admirable manner in which he provic a visit. .After tea the P.G.M. made a few Et, remarks and congratulated the officers cf ti. _ _ _</p>
        <p>and the Bowling Main Committee on the which they had achieved in their second main. prizes will be presented by the P.G.M. at a evening to be held on the Ist November next, will the date of the official visit of the District Office the Lodge. P.G. Wm. E. Clare acted as hon. secr. for the main. Scores :</p>
        <p>FIRST ROUND. Thomas Critclaley (3) l5 v John Inglis (7) ...... g Henry Critchley (4) H. Williams, junr. (4) C. Woolstencroft (5) Wm. E. Clare (3) l5 v Fred Ince (6) lf . Arthur Evans (5) Thos. Llewellyn (7) Jas. G. Hinde (7) Jas. A. Woodhead (6)... w.o. v Samuel Baldry (7) -7 Evan Stockton (4) l2 v John Bolesworth (2) 11! Henry Fogg (s)</p>
        <p>SECOND ROD). - . Frank Webster Henry Fogg l5 v H. Williams, se ...... 8, Wm. E. Clare H. Williams, jun l2 v Jas.A. Woodhead.., 15 Thos. Critobley Bye: Arthur Evans.</p>
        <p>THIRD ROUND. Arthur Evans Henry Forg. l5 v Jas. G Blade William Webb l4 v John Bolesworth ...... 15</p>
        <p>FOURTIT/A.II7ND. John Boleswortb Bye, Jas. A. Woodhead. FINAL. John Bolesworth</p>
