      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-09-18_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>_ PICTURES OF THE WEFAK,</head>
        <p>_ PICTURES OF THE WEFAK,</p>
        <p>LONDON TO MANCHESTER BY AEROPLANE, 1,21 r. S. F. Cody, Bri'ain's flying man, is to make an effort shortly to go by aeroplane itrot London to Manchester. He is to fly more or less by the London and North stern main line, passing to the cast of Birmingham, turning sharp west to avoid the tabYshire hills, north over the comparatively flat cou..try of Cheshire, and then aZ7ugh the Mersey valley into Manchester. The distance is about 200 mile, and '47. Cody expects to be atle to accomplish the task with:Nut descending. In our ZAltstration Mr. Cody is seen explaining thc working of his aeroplane to the Empress genie.</p>
