        <p>Local Oddfellowship. The second annual distribution of bowling Prl-1116 connection with the " Constitution" Lodge (1-t tII6Y Manchester Unity of Oddfellows took place 3,5 Pelican Hotel on Saturday evening.—T iere large gathering and the proceedings were bight,' 00 cessful. Bro. F. Buckley Mellor, N.G. presided, tair, Bro. J. Grounds, V.G., occupied the r, ,iee-A,peri3ls3.„ Among those present were the Mayor (i"",,f'ote' Forshaw), Bro. Robert Pierpoint, Prov. Grand G. F. Freeman, Bro. F. Webster, C.S, T.P.G.fch,""ctt„,lo' S. Steel, William Hollhook, J. H. Norbury, SY' J. Massey, and W. Daintith, P.G.s Fred Taylor, 0. Webster, W. Carter, W. King, Henry Taylor, ,(7., Warburton Steel, Wilfrid Taylor, T. Reddish, otlicrotc; Lester. -'Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart., regretting that he was unable to be present 00 Mr. Crosfield, M.P., telegraphed that lie,raellt. prevented from attending through another eng36'Contv The Mayor presented the prizes as follows Orci' cillor Steel's challenge cup and gold Ille(131'' ; Thomas Howard; 2, H. Savoury ;3, G. IfolbriVs.'esn'' J. A, Wood; 5, W. A. Warburton ; 0, J. W., :il, ' A 7, L. Williams; 8, J. W. Rigby • 9, W. IT. 1;7, IN-' T. S. Steel; 11, W. Holloway; 12, W. Leig',l Jarman.—Grand Master Freeman presented Wray; 14, R. Bennett; 15, F. Lloyd; ariLotitfl" emblem, handsomely framed, to Past Gran- ejisi 2-- Warburton Steel, who has passed through the pont/ of the Lodge.—The toast of the visitors was ree'ienr, to by Bro. Robert Pierpoint who said that fra osiciv societies must not allow themselves to be Plohe'6 ioter; and must not allow Government officialism t fere with them.—Other toasts were honoured enjoyable unusual programme was'subraitted.</p>
