        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— The BRIDGES COMMITTEE invite DESIGNS, SPECIFICATIONS, and TENDERS for a SINGLE- SeAN FERRO-CONCRETE BRIDGE across the river Mersey in Warrington, and training walls. .The Span is 134 feet between abutments. The Tenders to include the removal of the existing stone bridge. Conditions and particulars, with plans of site and existing bridge, may be obtained from the office of the Borough Engineer and Surveyor, Town Hall, Warring- ton, on and after Tuesday, the 21st inst., on payment of one guinea, which will be returned on receipt of a bona- fide tender. Cheques to be made payable to the Borough rreasurer, Warrington. Plans and renders, endorsed "Warrington Bridge," to be delivered at my office not later than 12 o'clock on October 26th. J. LYON WHITTLE, 16th September, 1909. Town Clerk.</p>
